      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Find $∇f(x,y,z),$  given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{1/2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{y}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{z}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(-\\frac{x}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}})i+(-\\frac{y}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}})j+(-\\frac{z}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}})k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}}(x\\,i+y\\,j+z\\,k)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
